{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "B1",
  "unit": 10,
  "title": "If it happens",
  "description": "Talk about what will happen, and what would happen.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Spanish has a conditional that English does not: the word would in a sentence like I would go is a real verb form in Spanish, hablaría. It is used for what would happen, and it is the polite way to say what you think should happen.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The conditional",
        "body": "The endings are -ía, -ías, -ía, -íamos, -íais, -ían. For -ar verbs they look like the imperfect of -er verbs: hablar, hablaría, hablarías, hablaría. For -er and -ir verbs they look the same: comer, comería; vivir, viviría. Ir is irregular: iría.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Yo iría a tu casa.",
            "en": "I would go to your house."
          },
          {
            "es": "¿Comerías conmigo?",
            "en": "Would you eat with me?"
          },
          {
            "es": "Viviría en el campo.",
            "en": "I would live in the countryside."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "If, then",
        "body": "Spanish uses si for if and no then, but the word order changes: the conditional comes first and si comes after it. Si tuviera tiempo, viajaría. If you put si first, as in English, it is wrong.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Si tuviera tiempo, viajaría.",
            "en": "If I had time, I would travel."
          },
          {
            "es": "Si hace buen tiempo, iremos a la playa.",
            "en": "If the weather is good, we will go to the beach."
          },
          {
            "es": "Si no llueve, saldremos.",
            "en": "If it does not rain, we will go out."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "What you think should happen",
        "body": "The conditional is also how you advise: deberías descansar. You should rest. Deberías comes from deber, which means to owe or must, so the idea is you owe yourself a rest.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Deberías dormir más.",
            "en": "You should sleep more."
          },
          {
            "es": "No deberías fumar.",
            "en": "You should not smoke."
          },
          {
            "es": "Deberíamos irnos.",
            "en": "We should go."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
